{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And Elohim blessed them</b> — This is an actual blessing. Therefore it is written concerning it, \"and Elohim said to them,\" whereas above (v. 22) it is written, \"and Elohim blessed them, saying (לֵאמֹר)\" — this teaches that the blessing is the utterance through which He implanted in them the power of reproduction, not a single statement in which they would be blessed." "<b>And fill the earth</b> — A blessing that the world would be filled with their abundance. In my opinion, He blessed them that they would fill the entire earth and that the nations would spread out to their families at the ends of the earth because of their abundance, and that they would not remain in one place, as the men of the generation of the Dispersion (דור הפלגה) intended." "<b>And subdue it</b> — He gave them power and dominion over the earth to do as they wish with beasts and creeping things and all crawling things of the dust, and to build and to uproot what is planted, and from its mountains to hew copper and the like. And this includes what He said, \"and over all the earth\" (Genesis 1:26)." "<b>And rule over the fish of the sea</b> — He said that they would also rule over the fish of the sea that are concealed from them, and over the birds of the sky that are not with them on the earth, and over every living creature, even the dangerous ones. And He arranged them according to their creation: the fish and the bird first, and the living creature afterward. And thus Scripture says (Psalms 8:7–9): \"You make him ruler over the works of Your hands; You have put all things under his feet: sheep and oxen, all of them, and also the beasts of the field, the birds of the sky, and the fish of the sea,\" etc. And our Sages drew a distinction between subjugation (כבישה) and dominion (רדיה):"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-21T22:15:22.128374805Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}